  "surprise": "P02 follow-up: tripling decoupled Muon weight decay (MUON_WD 0.01 -> 0.03; peak per-step shrinkage 1e-4 -> 3e-4, cumulative factor ~0.46 vs ~0.77) on incumbent 066-claude scored 335/285/362 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 319/293/335: exact means 327.333333 versus 315.666667, +11.67 (+3.7%); paired +16/-8/+27. Keep under the strictly-higher three-seed rule; no other-agent result was published during the run. Inside the registered -40 to +25 range and within seed noise (sd ~44 per seed), so read it as 'no harm, maybe small help', not an established effect. Pretraining cost nothing and showed no regularization signature: 4746/4761/4757 steps (066: 4760/4756/4786), final val loss 0.0923/0.0914/0.0967 vs 0.0932/0.0915/0.0956, end train/val gap 0.033/0.032/0.037 vs 0.034/0.032/0.037 (the predicted smaller gap did not appear), held-out greedy 0.9925/0.991/0.9905 vs 0.9895. The predicted better start failed: round-1 sample acc 0.061/0.043/0.051 vs 0.053/0.061/0.071 (higher on 1 of 3 seeds; 2 needed), and seed 2 lagged after round 2 (319 vs 480 targets). The gain came late, as in 064/066: round-4 acc 0.440/0.438/0.454 vs 0.433/0.417/0.449 and RL-solved 762/743/792 vs 743/716/772 (+19/+27/+20, every seed). That fits the plasticity half of the hypothesis (smaller Muon weights let the frozen RL AdamW move them further) better than a better initial policy, but weight norms were not logged, so it is unverified. Eval gains are mostly at 9 lines (187/149/216 vs 181/154/185); 10-line 17/15/25 vs 21/11/20. Totals 941-993 s, all ok. Next: MUON_WD 0.1 (10x) to test whether the RL-solved trend continues or attention sharpness breaks.",
